    "bio": "A Representative from Washington; born in Spokane, Spokane County, Wash., February 7, 1941; graduated from Pasco High School, Pasco, Wash., 1959; attended Columbia Basin College, Pasco, Wash., 1959-1961; attended Central Washington State University, Ellensburg, Wash., 1964; United States Army Reserves, 1963-1969; small businessman; member of the Washington state house of representatives, 1979-1987; delegate, Republican National Convention, 1976-1984; unsuccessful candidate for election to the United States House of Representatives in 1992; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Fourth and reelected to the nine succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1995-January 3, 2015); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Fourteenth Congress in 2014; chair, Committee on Standards of Official Conduct (One Hundred Ninth Congress); chair, Committee on Natural Resources (One Hundred Twelfth and One Hundred Thirteenth Congresses).",
